<item><title>Tunisia rises to 61st in English ranking as score falls eight points</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/tn/tunisia-rises-to-61st-in-english-ranking-as-score-falls-cd8662/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/tn/tunisia-rises-to-61st-in-english-ranking-as-score-falls-cd8662/</guid><category>Tunisia</category><description>The 2026 index puts Tunisia above the global average, but still in the low-proficiency category, with a 71-point gap between Ariana and Sidi Bouzid.</description><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:02:29 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/tn.jpg" length="31271" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/tn.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
